{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-flatness","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:quantum-flatness","kind":"definition","title":"Quantum flatness ($F_\\nabla = B$)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-connection","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-gauge-group"],"tags":["2-group","gauge-theory","instanton","quantum-flatness"],"defines":["quantum-flatness"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.IsQuantumFlat","text":"quantum-flatness.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-flatness.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:quantum-flatness\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B \\in \\Omega^2(A) \\otimes \\mathrm{Ad}(A)</code> be the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>-form datum of the inner-automorphism <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>-group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{INN}(G_q)</code>. The connection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\nabla</code> is <dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-quantum-flatness\">quantum flat</dfn> when its curvature equals the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2</code>-form datum: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">F_\\nabla = B</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-flatness.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"3.25.5"}
